1
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:12,100
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,900 --> 00:00:33,000
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:34,267 --> 00:00:35,200
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:41,467
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,533 --> 00:00:44,133
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:44,267 --> 00:00:45,267
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:46,767
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:46,900 --> 00:00:48,800
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:50,900 --> 00:00:51,900
[GUNSHOT]

10
00:00:52,867 --> 00:00:53,933
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:54,067 --> 00:00:55,733
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,833 --> 00:00:58,333
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:58,467 --> 00:01:00,567
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:01,433 --> 00:01:03,567
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:05,467 --> 00:01:06,667
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:07,567 --> 00:01:09,733
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:10,367 --> 00:01:11,867
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:13,167
- [TRUCK HORN HONKS]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:13,300 --> 00:01:14,900
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:20,633 --> 00:01:21,767
<i> I'm sorry because I'm the one</i>

21
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:24,000
<i>who brought bad luck
to our family.</i>

22
00:01:24,133 --> 00:01:25,400
<i> Because of me...</i>

23
00:01:25,533 --> 00:01:28,333
<i>I gave our father a wound
that I can never erase.</i>

24
00:01:28,467 --> 00:01:29,933
[SCREAMS] Help!

25
00:01:30,067 --> 00:01:31,800
<i> RJ!</i>

26
00:01:32,733 --> 00:01:34,800
<i>So this is what you do
to helpless people?</i>

27
00:01:34,933 --> 00:01:36,300
<i> You turn them into a business!</i>

28
00:01:36,433 --> 00:01:37,933
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [GRUNTING]

29
00:01:38,067 --> 00:01:40,333
- [KICK LANDS]
- [SLINGSHOT TWANGS]

30
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:41,667
<i> Mister Babot, you're safe now.</i>

31
00:01:41,800 --> 00:01:44,033
<i>Thank you
for saving my husband.</i>

32
00:01:44,167 --> 00:01:46,867
<i> Thank you for saving us.</i>

33
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:49,633
<i>I will repay you
for the rest of my life.</i>

34
00:01:49,767 --> 00:01:51,467
<i> Let's give her an hour.</i>

35
00:01:51,600 --> 00:01:54,833
<i>I'll find a way
to get her kicked out of here.</i>

36
00:01:54,967 --> 00:01:56,233
<i>- Hey!
- [BOTTLES BREAKING]</i>

37
00:01:56,367 --> 00:01:59,667
<i>If you have a problem with me,
say it to my face.</i>

38
00:01:59,800 --> 00:02:01,067
<i>- Fine!
- [SMACKS]</i>

39
00:02:01,567 --> 00:02:02,767
<i> That's enough!</i>

40
00:02:02,900 --> 00:02:05,500
<i> Stop it! Ibyang! Go home!</i>

41
00:02:06,867 --> 00:02:07,967
[IBYANG] Stop it!

42
00:02:08,100 --> 00:02:10,533
Why are you meddling
in our fights, anyway?!

43
00:02:10,667 --> 00:02:12,533
Romy, let go of me!

44
00:02:12,667 --> 00:02:14,533
I have to get back
at that woman!

45
00:02:14,700 --> 00:02:16,000
Stop it, that's enough!

46
00:02:16,133 --> 00:02:17,867
[IBYANG] I have to get back
at her!

47
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:19,100
[MATET] Shh, that's enough!

48
00:02:19,667 --> 00:02:21,833
- [IBYANG] Let me go!
- What happened?

49
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:23,867
- [MATET] Madam got
- Let me go!

50
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:26,233
into a fight with Miss Betchay.

51
00:02:26,367 --> 00:02:27,367
[DJANGO CHUCKLES]

52
00:02:27,500 --> 00:02:30,667
Why do you look like that?
Don't tell me you lost?

53
00:02:30,800 --> 00:02:32,833
If your dad hadn't stopped me...

54
00:02:32,967 --> 00:02:35,233
I'm sure they'd be grieving
over her by now!

55
00:02:35,367 --> 00:02:36,467
Then why did you go home?

56
00:02:36,600 --> 00:02:38,267
'Cause Paquito told her to.

57
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:42,033
Ibyang, since when did you
become Papa's minion?

58
00:02:43,700 --> 00:02:45,067
- Move it!
- Ouch!

59
00:02:45,200 --> 00:02:47,867
- I got hit, too!
- [DJANGO CHUCKLING]

60
00:02:48,033 --> 00:02:50,067
- [ROSANNA] Go on, girls.
- [WOMAN] Thank you, boss!

61
00:02:50,200 --> 00:02:51,500
Just my luck.

62
00:02:52,200 --> 00:02:55,800
[PAQUITO] Betchay,
what really is your problem?

63
00:02:55,933 --> 00:02:59,500
Over the years
we've been together...

64
00:02:59,633 --> 00:03:02,600
I'm always the one who gives.

65
00:03:02,733 --> 00:03:06,033
I'm always the one
who understands.

66
00:03:06,167 --> 00:03:10,400
I'm the one making sacrifices,
and I'm the one they blame?

67
00:03:11,200 --> 00:03:14,400
I'm the one working,
but I'm still the bad guy!

68
00:03:14,533 --> 00:03:16,167
The problem with you...

69
00:03:16,300 --> 00:03:21,900
...is you married someone
with a gangster son!

70
00:03:22,567 --> 00:03:26,133
Hey, Gabo's useful now!

71
00:03:26,267 --> 00:03:28,700
- He's got a job!
- What?

72
00:03:29,400 --> 00:03:34,733
You know, he paid
the hospital fees.

73
00:03:34,867 --> 00:03:36,333
- All of it?
- Mm-hmm!

74
00:03:36,467 --> 00:03:38,967
200,000 pesos?

75
00:03:39,800 --> 00:03:41,600
What kind of work does he have?

76
00:03:41,733 --> 00:03:43,667
- Well, I'm suspicious of it.
- Oh?

77
00:03:43,800 --> 00:03:46,200
- I think it's illegal work.
- Huh?

78
00:03:46,333 --> 00:03:49,367
'Cause Gabo never does
anything good!

79
00:03:49,500 --> 00:03:52,767
Maybe he mugged someone.
Or maybe...

80
00:03:53,533 --> 00:03:57,033
He kidnapped someone!
Or he stole!

81
00:03:59,300 --> 00:04:01,267
[DJANGO] So, should I
destroy Betchay?

82
00:04:01,400 --> 00:04:04,567
Ibyang, just say the word,
and I'll do it.

83
00:04:04,700 --> 00:04:06,533
I mean, I already shot
Gabo's father.

84
00:04:06,667 --> 00:04:08,400
I'll shoot his stepmother next.

85
00:04:08,533 --> 00:04:09,733
[DJANGO CHUCKLES]

86
00:04:09,867 --> 00:04:12,133
Let me finish our fight.

87
00:04:12,733 --> 00:04:14,467
We're just getting started.

88
00:04:15,433 --> 00:04:16,767
But that father of yours...

89
00:04:17,333 --> 00:04:19,733
We'll talk when he gets home.

90
00:04:19,867 --> 00:04:22,033
That Paquito might start
to think

91
00:04:22,167 --> 00:04:24,133
that because I'm not
his real wife,

92
00:04:24,267 --> 00:04:27,767
he can just embarrass me
in public.

93
00:04:27,933 --> 00:04:28,900
No way!

94
00:04:29,567 --> 00:04:31,533
He was the same with Mama
back then...

95
00:04:32,233 --> 00:04:34,367
...until she got tired and left.

96
00:04:34,967 --> 00:04:37,000
You think I can't leave
your father?

97
00:04:37,767 --> 00:04:39,167
I can if I want!

98
00:04:39,867 --> 00:04:41,000
Don't!

99
00:04:41,133 --> 00:04:44,233
You know, out of all the women
Papa has ever had...

100
00:04:44,867 --> 00:04:46,967
You're the only one
who can keep up with him!

101
00:04:47,567 --> 00:04:50,600
I'm even impressed with you!
We should drink to that!

102
00:04:50,733 --> 00:04:53,067
Come on! Being dramatic
doesn't suit you.

103
00:04:54,167 --> 00:04:55,433
Here.

104
00:04:55,567 --> 00:04:57,100
- [BOTTLES CLINK]
- That's it.

105
00:05:01,633 --> 00:05:02,800
I should get going.

106
00:05:02,933 --> 00:05:06,067
Wait! Wait, wait.
Wait a minute.

107
00:05:06,200 --> 00:05:11,200
Here. It's your pay for today.
I even included a tip!

108
00:05:11,333 --> 00:05:14,133
- Really? This is mine?
- Yeah! Yeah!

109
00:05:14,267 --> 00:05:17,100
Wow! Thank you.

110
00:05:17,233 --> 00:05:18,967
[PAQUITO STAMMERING]

111
00:05:19,100 --> 00:05:21,533
Uh, Betchay. Wait.

112
00:05:21,667 --> 00:05:24,700
Do you want to earn more?

113
00:05:24,833 --> 00:05:26,600
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

114
00:05:26,733 --> 00:05:28,367
Join our group.

115
00:05:28,500 --> 00:05:29,333
[CHUCKLES DRYLY]

116
00:05:29,467 --> 00:05:30,900
Come on now, Paquito.

117
00:05:31,033 --> 00:05:36,067
I'd never do anything illegal
just to make money.

118
00:05:36,233 --> 00:05:38,933
You won't be doing anything
of the sort.

119
00:05:39,067 --> 00:05:40,900
I've got a different job
for you.

120
00:05:41,033 --> 00:05:42,100
What are you saying?

121
00:05:42,233 --> 00:05:45,800
[PAQUITO] You've got skills
I can put to use.

122
00:05:46,467 --> 00:05:49,133
No stealing? No killing people?

123
00:05:49,267 --> 00:05:50,500
Absolutely not.

124
00:05:51,433 --> 00:05:52,800
And Betchay...

125
00:05:52,933 --> 00:05:56,467
You'll earn ten thousand pesos

126
00:05:56,600 --> 00:06:01,033
if you carry out
the task we give you.

127
00:06:02,367 --> 00:06:05,733
So what do you think?
Want to join our group?

128
00:06:06,267 --> 00:06:07,600
I'll think about it.

129
00:06:08,267 --> 00:06:09,433
[CHAIR SCRAPING]

130
00:06:09,567 --> 00:06:11,933
[MUSIC SWELLING]

131
00:06:12,067 --> 00:06:13,067
[MUSIC FADES]

132
00:06:14,233 --> 00:06:15,967
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

133
00:06:16,100 --> 00:06:20,100
[GUNSHOTS ECHOING]

134
00:06:20,233 --> 00:06:21,633
<i> -</i> [YOUNG RUDY]<i> Run!
<i> -</i> [YOUNG BELINDA]<i> Aah!</i></i>

135
00:06:21,767 --> 00:06:23,467
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

136
00:06:23,600 --> 00:06:24,733
<i> Come on, hurry!</i>

137
00:06:25,133 --> 00:06:27,000
Gabriel. Gabriel, listen to me.

138
00:06:27,133 --> 00:06:28,400
<i> Listen to Mommy, okay?</i>

139
00:06:28,533 --> 00:06:29,867
<i> Mommy loves you so much.</i>

140
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:32,300
<i>No matter what happens,
always stay good.</i>

141
00:06:32,433 --> 00:06:35,000
<i>Don't forget everything
I taught you, okay?</i>

142
00:06:35,133 --> 00:06:36,300
[YOUNG GABO]
<i> Okay, Mommy.</i>

143
00:06:36,433 --> 00:06:37,933
[YOUNG BELINDA]<i> Have mercy
</i> on my family! Take me instead!

144
00:06:38,067 --> 00:06:39,033
- [BLOW LANDS]
- [GUNSHOT]

145
00:06:39,167 --> 00:06:40,167
[SHOUTS] Ma!

146
00:06:40,300 --> 00:06:47,100
- [BREATHING HEAVILY]
- [GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

147
00:06:58,800 --> 00:07:01,000
[SCREAMS] Mommy!

148
00:07:02,833 --> 00:07:03,867
[YOUNG RUDY] Gabo...

149
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:05,967
<i>Son, are you having
nightmares again?</i>

150
00:07:06,100 --> 00:07:08,300
[VOICE BREAKING]
<i> It's Mommy...</i>

151
00:07:08,433 --> 00:07:09,867
<i> Me too, son.</i>

152
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:11,667
<i> I miss your mommy as well.</i>

153
00:07:11,800 --> 00:07:13,467
<i> Forgive me, son.</i>

154
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:15,467
<i> I couldn't save your mother.</i>

155
00:07:15,633 --> 00:07:16,900
<i> Please, forgive me.</i>

156
00:07:17,033 --> 00:07:20,100
[YOUNG GABO] I miss Mommy.

157
00:07:20,233 --> 00:07:27,267
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

158
00:07:29,100 --> 00:07:30,367
[DOOR CREAKS, THUDS]

159
00:07:41,367 --> 00:07:48,333
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

160
00:07:52,433 --> 00:07:53,500
[GABO INHALES DEEPLY]

161
00:07:56,033 --> 00:07:57,133
[BREATHES DEEPLY]

162
00:07:58,833 --> 00:07:59,800
[SNIFFLES]

163
00:08:03,400 --> 00:08:04,400
[GABO SIGHS]

164
00:08:06,167 --> 00:08:07,200
Pa.

165
00:08:11,600 --> 00:08:13,133
What are you still doing up?

166
00:08:13,267 --> 00:08:14,467
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

167
00:08:15,900 --> 00:08:17,967
I'm just getting some air, son.

168
00:08:20,133 --> 00:08:22,667
[STAMMERS] W-Why are you
still awake at this hour?

169
00:08:31,500 --> 00:08:34,267
The past still gives me
nightmares, Pa.

170
00:08:34,767 --> 00:08:37,600
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

171
00:08:37,733 --> 00:08:40,200
I can't get over what
happened to Mama.

172
00:08:40,900 --> 00:08:42,500
[SIGHS] You know, son...

173
00:08:44,400 --> 00:08:46,500
I know what's on your mind.

174
00:08:47,267 --> 00:08:49,067
You're thinking about...

175
00:08:49,967 --> 00:08:53,033
about how to take revenge
on those people.

176
00:08:53,167 --> 00:08:57,133
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

177
00:08:57,300 --> 00:08:58,833
Just stop, son.

178
00:09:01,433 --> 00:09:03,167
Forget about it.

179
00:09:04,533 --> 00:09:05,633
Don't...

180
00:09:05,767 --> 00:09:08,367
Don't gamble your life

181
00:09:09,400 --> 00:09:10,867
just for revenge.

182
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:12,200
[GABO] No, Pa.

183
00:09:12,633 --> 00:09:15,500
I have to find out
who killed my mother.

184
00:09:15,633 --> 00:09:17,000
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

185
00:09:17,133 --> 00:09:20,133
I have to get justice
for her death.

186
00:09:20,433 --> 00:09:21,567
[SIGHS HEAVILY]

187
00:09:22,467 --> 00:09:25,367
I want to know the persons
responsible for her death.

188
00:09:27,600 --> 00:09:29,467
Who killed my mother, Pa?

189
00:09:31,500 --> 00:09:32,433
Who?!

190
00:09:32,567 --> 00:09:34,167
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

191
00:09:34,300 --> 00:09:35,800
Pa, answer my question.

192
00:09:36,167 --> 00:09:38,767
Do you know the people
who killed my mother?

193
00:09:40,300 --> 00:09:41,433
Do you?!

194
00:09:44,800 --> 00:09:45,933
No, son.

195
00:09:46,067 --> 00:09:47,833
I-I have no idea.

196
00:09:48,267 --> 00:09:51,533
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

197
00:09:51,667 --> 00:09:56,700
[GABO BREATHING HEAVILY]

198
00:09:56,833 --> 00:09:58,367
I won't sit back
and do nothing, Pa.

199
00:09:59,833 --> 00:10:03,567
I won't let my mother's death
go without justice.

200
00:10:06,067 --> 00:10:07,667
I'll track them down.

201
00:10:07,800 --> 00:10:08,900
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

202
00:10:09,033 --> 00:10:11,267
I'll avenge my mother's death.

203
00:10:11,833 --> 00:10:13,833
Son, just let it all go.

204
00:10:15,333 --> 00:10:17,367
Don't... Don't get yourself
into danger.

205
00:10:18,067 --> 00:10:20,133
[STAMMERS]
I-If they come after you...

206
00:10:20,267 --> 00:10:23,267
I can't bear to lose you.

207
00:10:23,400 --> 00:10:25,833
I don't care who they are.

208
00:10:25,967 --> 00:10:26,800
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

209
00:10:26,933 --> 00:10:29,633
I won't stop until I find them.

210
00:10:30,533 --> 00:10:33,600
Not until justice is served
for my mother.

211
00:10:36,067 --> 00:10:37,633
I won't rest, Pa.

212
00:10:39,200 --> 00:10:40,867
I'll find them.

213
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:46,600
[MUSIC SWELLING]

214
00:10:46,733 --> 00:10:53,667
[MUSIC BECOMES THRILLING]

215
00:11:01,033 --> 00:11:02,767
[FOOTSTEPS RETREATING]

216
00:11:16,400 --> 00:11:18,067
- Django.
- Yes, Pa?

217
00:11:19,100 --> 00:11:22,467
Do you know
what Gabo's new job is?

218
00:11:23,800 --> 00:11:25,467
Who cares about that jerk?

219
00:11:25,600 --> 00:11:28,100
I don't care
what that bastard does.

220
00:11:28,233 --> 00:11:29,467
Find out what he does.

221
00:11:29,933 --> 00:11:36,267
Because, according to Betchay,
Gabo earned 200,000 pesos...

222
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:38,067
...in just one day.

223
00:11:38,200 --> 00:11:40,667
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

224
00:11:40,800 --> 00:11:44,100
What could be the reason
Gabo made that much money?

225
00:11:44,967 --> 00:11:46,600
He makes risky moves.

226
00:11:46,733 --> 00:11:51,100
He could've mugged a bank,
or robbed a pawnshop.

227
00:11:51,233 --> 00:11:53,233
It's so hard for us
to earn money,

228
00:11:53,367 --> 00:11:57,400
while Gabo gets money
that easily?

229
00:11:57,533 --> 00:12:00,400
That's why you have to
find out what he does, Django!

230
00:12:01,133 --> 00:12:05,700
Who knows, he might slowly
be robbing us of our income.

231
00:12:05,833 --> 00:12:07,800
One day,
we might just wake up...

232
00:12:08,333 --> 00:12:11,633
...and Gabo and his group
already control Ginintuang Lupa.

233
00:12:12,267 --> 00:12:15,900
I won't let that happen.
Gabo can't overpower us.

234
00:12:16,533 --> 00:12:18,367
He'll have to deal
with my fists first!

235
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:25,967
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

236
00:12:33,600 --> 00:12:38,367
[OBJECTS RUSTLING, THUMPING]

237
00:12:39,400 --> 00:12:41,800
Oh, Sam? You're going to work?

238
00:12:41,933 --> 00:12:46,967
But I booked a spa retreat
for you to de-stress,

239
00:12:47,100 --> 00:12:49,100
and bond with me!

240
00:12:49,833 --> 00:12:51,600
I need to go to the office.

241
00:12:51,733 --> 00:12:53,100
People from Internal Affairs
are there.

242
00:12:53,233 --> 00:12:58,033
They'll tell me
if they'll dismiss me or not.

243
00:12:59,867 --> 00:13:01,600
They can't dismiss you.

244
00:13:02,167 --> 00:13:04,700
You are a good agent!

245
00:13:05,267 --> 00:13:09,033
Who punched a criminal
who's in our custody.

246
00:13:09,167 --> 00:13:10,833
Well, I believe...

247
00:13:10,967 --> 00:13:13,600
not that I'm justifying
your actions,

248
00:13:13,733 --> 00:13:15,800
but I know there is a reason...

249
00:13:16,400 --> 00:13:20,733
...why you did it!
You will be fine.

250
00:13:21,500 --> 00:13:22,467
Okay?

251
00:13:23,100 --> 00:13:30,233
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

252
00:13:32,733 --> 00:13:35,733
Dad. I know aside from Sam,

253
00:13:35,867 --> 00:13:37,200
you already have
a lot of problems,

254
00:13:37,333 --> 00:13:40,167
one of which is Ginintuang Lupa.
Well, I just...

255
00:13:40,300 --> 00:13:42,800
...want you to know
that I am onto something.

256
00:13:42,933 --> 00:13:44,567
Wait, um...

257
00:13:46,200 --> 00:13:48,100
You'll visit the family of...

258
00:13:49,300 --> 00:13:50,967
...Rudy? Rudy Magtibay?

259
00:13:51,533 --> 00:13:53,600
Yes, Dad, the family
of the man who was shot.

260
00:13:54,200 --> 00:13:55,200
And...

261
00:13:57,733 --> 00:13:58,933
[MAX SIGHS]

262
00:13:59,067 --> 00:14:00,100
Please, Dad.

263
00:14:01,167 --> 00:14:02,700
Trust me on this one.

264
00:14:03,567 --> 00:14:07,833
Max, you know I believe in you.
But whatever you're planning...

265
00:14:10,333 --> 00:14:11,900
Don't be like Sam...

266
00:14:12,033 --> 00:14:13,833
...who's now dealing
with a problem she created.

267
00:14:13,967 --> 00:14:15,800
Don't be like her, please?

268
00:14:19,600 --> 00:14:21,967
[KAREN] I know what Sam
is going through.

269
00:14:22,100 --> 00:14:24,033
I can feel her hurt

270
00:14:24,167 --> 00:14:27,233
'cause I've only seen
her drink like that last night!

271
00:14:27,367 --> 00:14:28,933
We can't blame her.

272
00:14:29,100 --> 00:14:31,900
We worked so hard
to catch Mr. Chan,

273
00:14:32,033 --> 00:14:33,900
but she ended up suspended.

274
00:14:34,600 --> 00:14:35,567
[PIA] Oh?

275
00:14:36,300 --> 00:14:37,567
Where did you go last night?

276
00:14:38,133 --> 00:14:39,067
[SEBASTIAN CLEARS THROAT]

277
00:14:39,233 --> 00:14:41,367
[SEQIOA] Ma'am Pia,
it's nothing.

278
00:14:41,500 --> 00:14:42,867
We just went out
for some drinks.

279
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:45,167
Mm! You celebrated?

280
00:14:46,633 --> 00:14:47,767
But celebrated what?

281
00:14:48,600 --> 00:14:50,567
You catching Mr. Chan?

282
00:14:52,800 --> 00:14:55,167
It's not like that, Ma'am Pia.
Um...

283
00:14:55,300 --> 00:14:57,067
Jacinto's troubled
with her situation,

284
00:14:57,200 --> 00:14:59,767
- so we had drinks.
- Just her situation?

285
00:14:59,900 --> 00:15:01,667
You'll be in trouble, too!

286
00:15:02,533 --> 00:15:04,500
You're accomplices, aren't you?

287
00:15:04,633 --> 00:15:08,900
Now that Internal Affairs
will investigate Jacinto,

288
00:15:09,033 --> 00:15:12,833
you'll get entangled in this
when the truth comes out.

289
00:15:12,967 --> 00:15:17,933
Instead of reporting Jacinto,
what did you do?

290
00:15:18,900 --> 00:15:20,333
You sided with her!

291
00:15:20,467 --> 00:15:23,567
Because we knew our plan
will have a positive result.

292
00:15:23,700 --> 00:15:27,433
And that is correct, isn't it?
We caught Mr. Chan.

293
00:15:27,567 --> 00:15:29,533
It did have a positive result.

294
00:15:30,567 --> 00:15:31,933
Jacinto's suspended!

295
00:15:32,800 --> 00:15:36,667
Look, Jacinto's jeepney
is arriving,

296
00:15:36,833 --> 00:15:40,500
and it's headed to the dumps!
You should all ride it, hm?

297
00:15:46,100 --> 00:15:47,967
Here, I already signed this.
It's done.

298
00:15:48,100 --> 00:15:49,500
- Sir, thank you.
- Alright.

299
00:15:50,233 --> 00:15:51,500
- [POLICE 1] Good morning, sir.
- [POLICE 2] Good morning, sir.

300
00:15:51,633 --> 00:15:53,600
- Good morning.
- [SEBASTIAN] Director!

301
00:15:53,733 --> 00:15:54,867
- Yes?
- Sir.

302
00:15:55,800 --> 00:15:56,967
Can we talk?

303
00:15:58,200 --> 00:16:00,100
[DELGADO] You seem troubled.

304
00:16:00,700 --> 00:16:02,567
[SEBASTIAN] Because, sir,
Internal Affairs

305
00:16:02,700 --> 00:16:04,467
will interview
my almost-girlfriend.

306
00:16:04,600 --> 00:16:07,367
[DELGADO] Almost-girlfriend?
Who? Sam?

307
00:16:07,500 --> 00:16:08,667
Hm.

308
00:16:08,833 --> 00:16:11,600
She's getting interviewed later
because of what she did.

309
00:16:11,733 --> 00:16:13,833
[SEBASTIAN] Sir,
she's already suspended,

310
00:16:13,967 --> 00:16:15,300
but there's still an interview?

311
00:16:15,767 --> 00:16:16,733
For what?

312
00:16:16,867 --> 00:16:17,733
To pressure her?

313
00:16:17,867 --> 00:16:18,767
Sir, remember,

314
00:16:18,900 --> 00:16:20,333
if Sam didn't take action,

315
00:16:20,467 --> 00:16:22,267
we wouldn't have been able
to catch Mr. Chan.

316
00:16:22,400 --> 00:16:23,633
Sebastian.

317
00:16:23,867 --> 00:16:28,033
This is what we do to people
who don't follow the protocol.

318
00:16:28,500 --> 00:16:29,767
I know that, sir.

319
00:16:29,900 --> 00:16:33,133
But if we're going
to let internal affairs

320
00:16:33,267 --> 00:16:34,633
interview Sam,

321
00:16:34,767 --> 00:16:38,967
they should let Sam
explain her side.

322
00:16:39,100 --> 00:16:42,033
Actually, sir, NCIA
shouldn't be focusing on Sam.

323
00:16:42,200 --> 00:16:43,167
They should focus on Mr. Chan.

324
00:16:43,300 --> 00:16:44,800
We need to make him talk.

325
00:16:44,933 --> 00:16:47,167
We will be able to do that.

326
00:16:47,300 --> 00:16:50,167
We just have to be sure
that he is safe.

327
00:16:50,300 --> 00:16:53,000
So we will move him
to a safe house.

328
00:16:53,133 --> 00:16:57,467
Because Mr. Chan
is requesting to be part

329
00:16:58,033 --> 00:17:00,067
of the witness
protection program.

330
00:17:00,200 --> 00:17:01,400
Is that so, sir?

331
00:17:02,033 --> 00:17:04,067
Then I'm going
to escort Mr. Chan.

332
00:17:04,200 --> 00:17:07,100
I'll do that to protect
Sam's trump card.

333
00:17:07,233 --> 00:17:09,467
You can't get near Mr. Chan.

334
00:17:09,600 --> 00:17:11,167
Because you have
a close connection

335
00:17:11,300 --> 00:17:13,667
to the group
that violated the protocol.

336
00:17:14,700 --> 00:17:16,567
Almost girlfriend.

337
00:17:18,567 --> 00:17:19,567
Right?

338
00:17:20,067 --> 00:17:21,133
Almost.

339
00:17:21,267 --> 00:17:27,533
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

340
00:17:30,567 --> 00:17:35,233
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

341
00:17:36,700 --> 00:17:38,667
<i>Have mercy on my family.
Take me instead.</i>

342
00:17:38,800 --> 00:17:40,233
[YOUNG BELINDA WHIMPERS,
SCREAMS]

343
00:17:41,200 --> 00:17:42,333
[GUNSHOTS]

344
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:45,533
[GABO]<i> They deprived my mom
</i> of justice.

345
00:17:47,067 --> 00:17:50,133
<i>But we are not the only ones
experiencing this cruelty.</i>

346
00:17:52,233 --> 00:17:56,200
<i>A lot of poor people
go through the same thing.</i>

347
00:17:58,333 --> 00:18:00,267
<i> It needs to stop.</i>

348
00:18:02,300 --> 00:18:04,467
<i>There's only one person
who can help me.</i>

349
00:18:04,600 --> 00:18:11,567
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

350
00:18:26,900 --> 00:18:28,933
[PAPANG]<i> Our country
</i> is too chaotic.

351
00:18:29,067 --> 00:18:31,533
<i> The chaos around is rampant.</i>

352
00:18:31,667 --> 00:18:32,933
[TOMAS] Even our government

353
00:18:33,067 --> 00:18:35,633
<i>can't contain the surge
of criminals anymore.</i>

354
00:18:35,767 --> 00:18:37,433
<i> That's why Anino is here.</i>

355
00:18:37,567 --> 00:18:41,933
<i> To help clean our country.</i>

356
00:18:42,067 --> 00:18:49,033
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

357
00:18:52,067 --> 00:18:53,133
[DRAWER CLOSES]

358
00:18:57,233 --> 00:19:02,167
[MUSIC BECOMES STIRRING]

359
00:19:02,300 --> 00:19:03,367
[CLANKS]

360
00:19:05,033 --> 00:19:06,900
[RUBBER BAND STRETCHES]

361
00:19:14,400 --> 00:19:15,500
Gabo, join us.

362
00:19:15,500 --> 00:19:16,967
Come on, have your breakfast.

363
00:19:16,967 --> 00:19:18,100
[GABO] Good morning.

364
00:19:18,400 --> 00:19:21,333
- [DANTE] Eat with us.
- So, do you have work today?

365
00:19:22,167 --> 00:19:23,133
Uh...

366
00:19:23,133 --> 00:19:24,867
I'm not sure, Auntie.

367
00:19:24,867 --> 00:19:28,533
I'm waiting for their call
to see if I'm scheduled today.

368
00:19:28,567 --> 00:19:29,933
- Mm-hmm.
- [WATER SLOSHING]

369
00:19:29,933 --> 00:19:32,533
Gabo, what sort of job
did you end up taking?

370
00:19:32,533 --> 00:19:35,267
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

371
00:19:35,267 --> 00:19:36,600
You see, Pa...

372
00:19:36,967 --> 00:19:39,333
It's hard to explain.

373
00:19:39,667 --> 00:19:41,267
I do a lot of things.

374
00:19:41,267 --> 00:19:45,800
Sometimes they ask me
to deliver packages,

375
00:19:45,800 --> 00:19:50,167
and other times they ask me
to find certain people.

376
00:19:52,400 --> 00:19:55,200
[TEKLA] Hey, we're finally here!
Ready to join for breakfast!

377
00:19:55,200 --> 00:19:57,267
- It's a beautiful morning!
- Good morning!

378
00:19:57,267 --> 00:19:59,333
- Gabo, what's up?
- Alright, sure thing.

379
00:19:59,333 --> 00:20:01,867
- Breakfast is our first stop.
- Come on, join us here.

380
00:20:01,900 --> 00:20:02,967
Grab some bread.

381
00:20:02,967 --> 00:20:04,467
This is exactly why
we came here.

382
00:20:04,467 --> 00:20:05,633
I'm starving.

383
00:20:05,633 --> 00:20:07,233
- [MAMENG CHUCKLES]
- Hey, give me some!

384
00:20:07,667 --> 00:20:08,833
[TEKLA] Gabo.

385
00:20:09,033 --> 00:20:11,167
- Got a new gig lined up for us?
- I can't say for sure.

386
00:20:11,500 --> 00:20:12,667
Well, I'm still...

387
00:20:13,333 --> 00:20:14,633
I'm still waiting
for their call.

388
00:20:14,633 --> 00:20:15,767
What a bummer.

389
00:20:15,767 --> 00:20:18,400
I hope they ring soon
so we can earn some cash.

390
00:20:18,400 --> 00:20:19,800
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

391
00:20:19,800 --> 00:20:21,267
Gabo, count us in, okay?

392
00:20:21,267 --> 00:20:23,000
We don't want to miss out
this time.

393
00:20:23,333 --> 00:20:24,533
[IPE] There you go again.

394
00:20:24,533 --> 00:20:27,067
You have no faith in Gabo
at all.

395
00:20:27,067 --> 00:20:29,067
He's not the type
to cheat you out of money!

396
00:20:29,067 --> 00:20:30,400
- [TEKLA] Exactly!
- [DANTE] Shh, quiet!

397
00:20:30,800 --> 00:20:32,567
[BETCHAY] What the hell?!

398
00:20:32,567 --> 00:20:36,833
So much noise this early
in the morning!

399
00:20:37,633 --> 00:20:39,233
Do we have any ice here?

400
00:20:39,833 --> 00:20:41,300
Buy some ice for her

401
00:20:41,300 --> 00:20:43,867
so he can freshen up
and chill out.

402
00:20:44,267 --> 00:20:45,333
[DANTE] I'm on it.

403
00:20:45,667 --> 00:20:46,833
[LOUD THUD]

404
00:20:47,767 --> 00:20:50,567
[BETCHAY, DRYLY] Money for your
maintenance meds, sir.

405
00:20:50,567 --> 00:20:54,700
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

406
00:20:54,700 --> 00:20:55,767
[BETCHAY SCOFFS]

407
00:20:55,767 --> 00:20:57,667
The whole gang is here again.

408
00:20:58,767 --> 00:21:00,800
Taking food that's not yours.

409
00:21:00,800 --> 00:21:04,567
Do you even realize the price
behind that food?

410
00:21:04,567 --> 00:21:06,367
It's my sweat and blood!

411
00:21:06,900 --> 00:21:09,333
- I worked myself to the bone!
- [RUDY] That's enough!

412
00:21:09,367 --> 00:21:10,667
[CHAIR RATTLING, THUDS]

413
00:21:11,033 --> 00:21:12,100
[MAMENG] Rudy...

414
00:21:12,100 --> 00:21:13,900
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

415
00:21:13,900 --> 00:21:14,900
Rudy...

416
00:21:19,600 --> 00:21:20,633
[BANGS ON SCREEN DOOR]

417
00:21:21,900 --> 00:21:22,867
[SCREEN DOOR SLAMS]

418
00:21:28,867 --> 00:21:30,867
Auntie, we'll be outside.

419
00:21:32,333 --> 00:21:35,500
[TEKLA] Right, let's go.
It's too hot in here right now.

420
00:21:35,733 --> 00:21:38,567
It's really hot in here because
there's no air conditioner!

421
00:21:39,600 --> 00:21:42,067
- [TOLITS] Move it!
- Cramming in here doesn't help!

422
00:21:43,767 --> 00:21:46,000
She's really unbearable.

423
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:48,833
Gabo, why is she always
pissed at us?

424
00:21:49,200 --> 00:21:50,733
[BONG] How wouldn't she be?

425
00:21:50,733 --> 00:21:54,300
Someone here eats like crazy,
just demolishing Gabo's food.

426
00:21:54,300 --> 00:21:55,633
[DABOY]
It's just a bit, though...

427
00:21:55,633 --> 00:21:56,800
[TEKLA]
That's what you call a bit?

428
00:21:57,367 --> 00:21:58,867
You'll get used to it.

429
00:21:58,867 --> 00:22:00,433
That's just how she is.

430
00:22:00,433 --> 00:22:01,800
Try to understand her.

431
00:22:01,800 --> 00:22:04,333
[BINO] So, Gabo,
is there a gig or not?

432
00:22:04,333 --> 00:22:06,100
[TOLITS] Any way to make money?

433
00:22:06,500 --> 00:22:07,600
Not yet.

434
00:22:07,900 --> 00:22:09,300
They haven't called me yet.

435
00:22:09,300 --> 00:22:10,633
Okay, here's what we'll do.

436
00:22:10,633 --> 00:22:12,833
Let's just meet up later, okay?

437
00:22:12,833 --> 00:22:14,067
Gabo, we'll get going now.

438
00:22:14,067 --> 00:22:15,567
- Mmm, sure.
- Come on, let's go.

439
00:22:15,600 --> 00:22:16,633
Let's not waste the day.

440
00:22:16,633 --> 00:22:21,067
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

441
00:22:21,067 --> 00:22:22,133
Excuse me.

442
00:22:27,400 --> 00:22:28,467
Pa.

443
00:22:29,833 --> 00:22:31,200
Is your wound still painful?

444
00:22:31,200 --> 00:22:33,133
It's okay now.
It's starting to heal a bit.

445
00:22:34,000 --> 00:22:36,300
[BADONG] Rudy, the motorcycle's
all fixed up now.

446
00:22:36,600 --> 00:22:38,100
[ELTON]
What's the total bill, Badong?

447
00:22:38,100 --> 00:22:39,933
[BADONG] It's 4,700 pesos,
Mister Elton. All-in.

448
00:22:39,933 --> 00:22:42,067
That's for everything?
Put it here.

449
00:22:43,767 --> 00:22:44,933
Be careful with it.

450
00:22:45,500 --> 00:22:47,300
[KICKSTAND RATTLING]

451
00:22:48,300 --> 00:22:49,667
- Thanks.
- Mister Elton.

452
00:22:50,533 --> 00:22:53,833
Here's the payment
for the bike repair.

453
00:22:53,833 --> 00:22:54,967
That's 5,000 pesos.

454
00:22:55,733 --> 00:22:56,767
It's too much.

455
00:22:57,267 --> 00:22:58,767
You can keep the change.

456
00:22:59,367 --> 00:23:00,467
Thanks.

457
00:23:01,500 --> 00:23:04,167
[RUDY] Gabo, I told you
I'd handle the bill.

458
00:23:04,567 --> 00:23:05,567
It's fine, Pa.

459
00:23:05,567 --> 00:23:07,433
I still have some cash, anyway.

460
00:23:07,433 --> 00:23:09,167
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

461
00:23:09,167 --> 00:23:10,300
By the way, Pa...

462
00:23:10,800 --> 00:23:11,833
For your maintenance meds.

463
00:23:11,833 --> 00:23:13,567
- No, no, I can't take that.
- Please, Pa.

464
00:23:13,567 --> 00:23:15,467
That's for you.
I've got some cash remaining.

465
00:23:16,300 --> 00:23:17,633
Thank you.

466
00:23:18,733 --> 00:23:20,233
Where are you going?

467
00:23:20,233 --> 00:23:22,067
I was going to ask a favor.

468
00:23:22,100 --> 00:23:27,700
Can I borrow the bike again
to get to work?

469
00:23:27,700 --> 00:23:30,567
I promise, Pa, I'll be...

470
00:23:31,033 --> 00:23:32,700
I'll be careful.
I won't break it.

471
00:23:32,700 --> 00:23:34,333
You promise
you'll take care of it?

472
00:23:34,333 --> 00:23:36,133
- Yes, Pa.
- Alright, then.

473
00:23:36,133 --> 00:23:40,533
[THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING]

474
00:23:40,533 --> 00:23:41,533
Mister Elton.

475
00:23:42,100 --> 00:23:44,367
I already asked
Papa's permission...

476
00:23:44,367 --> 00:23:46,167
I'll just borrow the bike again.

477
00:23:46,167 --> 00:23:48,400
Where are you headed? The bike
might get messed up again!

478
00:23:48,400 --> 00:23:49,667
it was just repaired!

479
00:23:50,100 --> 00:23:52,200
Elton, let him use it.

480
00:23:52,733 --> 00:23:55,033
He promised that
he'll take care of it. Go on.

481
00:23:55,033 --> 00:23:56,500
- It's okay, son.
- Fine, Rudy.

482
00:23:56,533 --> 00:23:58,500
[THRILLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

483
00:23:58,500 --> 00:23:59,567
[GABO EXHALES]

484
00:24:00,200 --> 00:24:01,200
Take care.

485
00:24:01,633 --> 00:24:02,600
I will, Pa.

486
00:24:03,300 --> 00:24:04,333
Mister Elton.

487
00:24:04,333 --> 00:24:05,633
[ENGINE ROARING]

488
00:24:05,633 --> 00:24:07,233
[ENGINE REVVING]

489
00:24:07,233 --> 00:24:09,167
- [TEKLA] Stay safe, Gabo!
- We'll be right here!

490
00:24:11,267 --> 00:24:12,633
- Agent Chua.
- Yes, ma'am?

491
00:24:12,633 --> 00:24:14,500
Are the Internal Affairs people
here already?

492
00:24:14,500 --> 00:24:16,033
[AGENT CHUA]
They haven't arrived yet, ma'am.

493
00:24:16,733 --> 00:24:18,033
- Okay, thank you.
- Sure.

494
00:24:18,033 --> 00:24:24,867
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

495
00:24:24,867 --> 00:24:26,433
You're brave.

496
00:24:26,933 --> 00:24:28,467
I'll give you that.

497
00:24:29,100 --> 00:24:32,200
You really came here
to face the consequences?

498
00:24:33,000 --> 00:24:35,233
I'm only fulfilling part
of my duty.

499
00:24:35,233 --> 00:24:37,100
I'm here to undergo
a fair assessment

500
00:24:37,100 --> 00:24:39,767
and have my actions verified.

501
00:24:39,767 --> 00:24:41,200
Make the most out of it.

502
00:24:41,733 --> 00:24:43,000
For all we know,

503
00:24:43,600 --> 00:24:45,033
this might be your last time.

504
00:24:45,033 --> 00:24:46,500
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

505
00:24:46,500 --> 00:24:50,400
There's been far too much
chaos here,

506
00:24:50,400 --> 00:24:52,067
and it's all your fault.

507
00:24:52,733 --> 00:24:56,133
Tiger made an attempt
on Mr. Chan.

508
00:24:57,867 --> 00:25:00,733
The case is getting more
and more complicated

509
00:25:00,733 --> 00:25:02,433
because of you, Jacinto.

510
00:25:03,433 --> 00:25:06,000
This agency would be better off
without you.

511
00:25:16,500 --> 00:25:21,300
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

512
00:25:21,433 --> 00:25:22,800
[MOTORCYCLE ENGINE REVS]

513
00:25:37,633 --> 00:25:44,600
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

514
00:25:48,833 --> 00:25:50,033
[MOTORCYCLE ENGINE REVS]

515
00:25:58,967 --> 00:26:00,100
[WOMAN] Jeepney!

516
00:26:13,467 --> 00:26:14,967
[JEEPNEY WHOOSHES]

517
00:26:15,100 --> 00:26:16,567
[JEEPNEY, MOTORCYCLE
ENGINE REVVING]

518
00:26:28,767 --> 00:26:31,367
Here's our fare.
For two people, please.

519
00:26:33,867 --> 00:26:40,833
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

520
00:26:45,533 --> 00:26:46,800
[TIRES SCREECHING]

521
00:26:50,533 --> 00:26:51,767
[WOMAN] Be careful, dear.

522
00:26:53,667 --> 00:26:54,900
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

523
00:26:55,633 --> 00:26:58,733
Where would you like to eat
once we're done with enrollment?

524
00:26:58,867 --> 00:27:02,900
Let's go to
our favorite place, Ma.

525
00:27:05,400 --> 00:27:07,400
[YOUNG GABO] I love you, Mommy.

526
00:27:07,867 --> 00:27:09,067
[YOUNG BELINDA] I love you.

527
00:27:09,467 --> 00:27:10,900
[WOMAN] The restaurant
you love eating at?

528
00:27:11,033 --> 00:27:13,267
- [KID] Yes, Ma!
- [WOMAN] Okay.

529
00:27:22,933 --> 00:27:29,900
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

530
00:27:44,933 --> 00:27:50,433
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

531
00:27:50,600 --> 00:27:53,433
We will buy you
new school supplies.

532
00:28:06,500 --> 00:28:07,800
Walk faster, dear.

533
00:28:10,600 --> 00:28:11,633
Hurry up, son!

534
00:28:11,767 --> 00:28:13,033
- Run, son! [SCREAMS]
- [KID WHIMPERS] Ma...

535
00:28:13,167 --> 00:28:14,300
[GATE CLANKS]

536
00:28:14,433 --> 00:28:16,200
- [KID WHIMPERS] Help!
- Help!

537
00:28:17,600 --> 00:28:21,000
- [MOTORCYCLE ENGINE REVVING]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

538
00:28:22,967 --> 00:28:24,300
- Help!
- [KID CRYING]

539
00:28:24,433 --> 00:28:26,233
- Give us your bag!
- Give it!

540
00:28:26,367 --> 00:28:27,533
- [KID SOBBING] Mama!
- Hand it here!

541
00:28:27,667 --> 00:28:28,967
[KID CRYING]

542
00:28:29,100 --> 00:28:30,067
[GOON 1] Lift her up!

543
00:28:30,500 --> 00:28:32,133
- My son!
- [GOON 2] Give me that!

544
00:28:32,267 --> 00:28:33,500
- [SOBBING]
- [INDISTINCT SCREAMING]

545
00:28:33,633 --> 00:28:34,867
- [GOON 1 GRUNTS]
- [GUNSHOT]

546
00:28:35,400 --> 00:28:36,233
[KID] Ma!

547
00:28:36,367 --> 00:28:39,167
[MOTORCYCLE ENGINE REVVING]

548
00:28:39,300 --> 00:28:41,400
[CRYING] Ma! Ma!

549
00:28:41,533 --> 00:28:44,100
Let's go! Hurry, come on!

550
00:28:44,233 --> 00:28:47,067
- [MOTORCYCLE ENGINE REVVING]
- [GABO SCREAMING]

551
00:28:48,367 --> 00:28:49,333
[THUDDING]

552
00:28:49,467 --> 00:28:50,700
Ah!

553
00:28:52,933 --> 00:28:54,733
[KID] Help!

554
00:28:57,267 --> 00:28:58,900
- [COUGHING]
- Help us!

555
00:28:59,033 --> 00:29:00,167
Help!

556
00:29:01,000 --> 00:29:03,000
- [BLOW LANDS]
- [GUNSHOT]

557
00:29:03,133 --> 00:29:10,200
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

558
00:29:12,967 --> 00:29:14,600
<i> They are very influential.</i>

559
00:29:14,733 --> 00:29:17,033
<i>They'll use all their money
and all their connections.</i>

560
00:29:17,100 --> 00:29:19,000
<i>They will do everything to get
their son out of jail.</i>

561
00:29:19,133 --> 00:29:22,033
<i> Victor, you are going down!</i>

562
00:29:22,167 --> 00:29:26,400
Make sure you'll bring Mr. Chan
<i> to the safe house safely.</i>

563
00:29:26,533 --> 00:29:28,400
<i> Our target is Mr. Chan.</i>

564
00:29:28,533 --> 00:29:30,767
<i>Eliminate anyone who
will try to stop you.</i>

565
00:29:30,933 --> 00:29:32,067
<i> So, you're suspending, huh?</i>

566
00:29:32,200 --> 00:29:33,167
<i> We might get suspended too.</i>

567
00:29:33,300 --> 00:29:34,467
<i>I'd be fine
with only a suspension.</i>

568
00:29:34,600 --> 00:29:36,300
<i>But what if we lost
everything we worked hard on?</i>

569
00:29:36,433 --> 00:29:39,100
I thought you already understood
<i> that it wasn't Sam's fault?</i>

570
00:29:41,600 --> 00:29:42,633
[KICK LANDS]

571
00:29:43,800 --> 00:29:44,867
- [BLOW LANDS]
- [GRUNTING]

572
00:29:45,000 --> 00:29:46,100
<i>- Ah!
- [BLOW LANDS]</i>

573
00:29:47,133 --> 00:29:49,000
<i> Please help my mom!</i>

574
00:29:49,133 --> 00:29:50,000
<i> Help!</i>

575
00:29:50,133 --> 00:29:51,033
<i> Help us!</i>

576
00:29:51,167 --> 00:29:53,033
<i>- What happened?
- She was shot.</i>
